CORE
main.c
--show-struct-alignment
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^WARNING: declaration of structure narrow at file main\.c line 1$
^members a and b might interfere$
^WARNING: declaration of structure pad at file main\.c line 11$
^members c and s might interfere$
^WARNING: declaration of structure groups at file main\.c line 16$
^members g1 and g2 might interfere$
^members g1 and g3 might interfere$
^members g1 and g4 might interfere$
^members h1 and h2 might interfere$
^members h1 and h3 might interfere$
^WARNING: declaration of structure tail at file main\.c line 28$
^members t1 and t2 might interfere$
^members t1 and t3 might interfere$
--
^warning: ignoring
structure wide
members x and y
\$pad
^members (g2|g3|h2|t2) and
--
Members that fit in a single memory operand (an int) may interfere, which a and
b do, while x and y do not. The padding between c and s counts towards the
size of the memory operand, but is not reported as a member. Each group of
members that fit in a single memory operand is reported once, relative to its
first member: pairs that start from another member of the same group, such as
g2 and g3, h2 and h3, or t2 and t3, are not reported.
